/ Audit is the run-wide accumulator of every observed error (per debug.md: "Run-wide accumulator of every error.
/ Survives Pop."). Every error is recorded — the 4 inner throws (each handled) and the fourth, unhandled one the
/ outer handler catches. How many call frames record an error as it propagates is not promised, so the fourth is
/ asked for at least once, not counted.
TestAuditAccumulatesHandledAndUnhandledErrors
- set %items% = ["a", "b", "c", "d"]
- foreach %items%, call ThrowItem item=%item%, on error set %finalCaught% = true
- assert %finalCaught% is true
- set %audit% = %!call.Audit%
- filter %audit% where Key equals 'ItemFailed', write to %itemFailed%
- list.count %itemFailed%, write to %itemFailedCount%
- assert %itemFailedCount% equals 4
- list.any %audit% where Key equals 'Fourth', write to %hasFourth%
- assert %hasFourth% is true
